@page "/mentor-requests"
@layout AppLayout
@attribute [Authorize(Roles = Roles.Mentor + "," + Roles.Admin + "," + Roles.Staff)]
@namespace AuthWithAdmin.Client.Pages.Mentor
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using AuthWithAdmin.Client.Components
@using AuthWithAdmin.Client.Services
@using AuthWithAdmin.Shared.AuthSharedModels
@inject IProjectRequestsService RequestsService
@inject IMentorAttentionService Attention
@inject IRequestTypesService RequestTypesService

@*
    ── בקשות — the mentor's request queue ──────────────────────────────────

    SPLIT WORKSPACE, on the shared `rqw-*` skeleton
    (Client/wwwroot/css/motiva-request-workspace.css): page header with the
    title at the reading end and a compact KPI summary opposite it, the queue
    on the RIGHT scrolling inside itself, the selected request's record filling
    the LEFT. Nothing scrolls at page level. That skeleton is shared with the
    lecturer queue and is STRUCTURE ONLY — every question of which requests
    this page shows, what its buckets are called and what may be done to them
    is answered here and only here.

    THIS SUPERSEDES THE EXPAND-IN-PLACE LAYOUT drawn by
    design/design-system/Motiva Mentor Requests.dc.html, along with that file's
    "no KPI strip" rule, on an explicit product decision to run one request
    workspace across roles. What the reference still governs is this screen's
    own vocabulary — the four buckets, their names, the leading dot's four
    roles, the type menu — all of which are kept below.

    DATA. GET api/project-requests is already mentor-scoped server-side:
    ProjectRequestsController.GetAll appends
    `WHERE r.ProjectId IN (SELECT ProjectId FROM ProjectMentors WHERE UserId=@UserId)`
    for a Mentor-only caller. No client-side filter stands in for that, and no
    new endpoint was added for this screen.

    WHAT A MENTOR MAY ACTUALLY DO — and therefore what this page offers.
    The server gives a mentor exactly one decision:
    POST /api/project-requests/{id}/mentor-recommendation, [Authorize(Mentor)],
    gated on PendingMentorRecommendation. /handle and PATCH are Admin+Staff
    only, /reply requires team membership, and /extension/decision explicitly
    rejects Stage="Mentor". So the workspace hosts MentorRequestDetail
    unchanged — it already draws the recommendation form and nothing else —
    and the lecturer's אישור / דחייה / החזרה להשלמה never appear here.

    BUCKETS are MentorRequestBuckets.Of(), the mentor's four-way split, used
    verbatim and unchanged. The three pills fold those four:

        להמלצתך        = AwaitingMentor   = PendingMentorRecommendation
        ממתין לאחרים   = WithLecturer     = everything else (New, InProgress,
                                            WaitingForStaff,
                                            PendingLecturerDecision, and any
                                            status added later)
                       + AwaitingTeam     = NeedsInfo
        טופלו          = Closed           = Resolved, Closed

    The middle pill said "בטיפול" and now says "ממתין לאחרים". That is a
    correction, not a preference: "בטיפול" reads most naturally on a mentor's
    own queue as "being handled by you", and the mentor holds nothing in it —
    the one endpoint a mentor has is gated on PendingMentorRecommendation,
    which is the OTHER pill. See LaneLabel for the full argument.

    ORDERING puts the requests the mentor actually owns first — bucket order is
    descending urgency for a mentor — then newest activity within each. It
    still runs inside a lane, so it only separates WithLecturer from
    AwaitingTeam within ממתין לאחרים.

    THE ROW SAYS WHAT THE LECTURER QUEUE'S ROW SAYS, and nothing more: the
    request type, the title, and the team · project it belongs to. The
    submitter's name, the leading status dot, the holding phrase and
    "עדכון אחרון · dd.MM" all came off. Every one of them either restated the
    selected pill or was a value nobody acts on from a list; all of them are
    still on the opened record, which is where a mentor reads detail.

    CARRIED OVER: the ?requestId= deep link a notification arrives on, and
    MarkRead on open (inside MentorRequestDetail).
    NOT CARRIED OVER: the reference's ↑/↓ stepper and its expand-in-place card,
    both of which only existed to move between rows that replaced themselves.
*@

<div class="rqw-page" dir="rtl">

    <!-- ── PAGE HEADER ── -->
    <div class="rqw-header">
        <h1 class="rqw-title">בקשות</h1>
    </div>

    @if (_loading)
    {
        <MLoadingState Label="טוענת בקשות…" />
    }
    else if (_loadError)
    {
        <MEmptyState Live="true"
                     Title="לא הצלחנו לטעון את הבקשות"
                     Description="ייתכן שיש תקלת רשת זמנית. אפשר לנסות שוב.">
            <Action>
                <MButton Variant="MButton.ButtonVariant.Secondary" OnClick="LoadAsync">נסי שוב</MButton>
            </Action>
        </MEmptyState>
    }
    else if (_all.Count == 0)
    {
        <MEmptyState Title="אין בקשות בפרויקטים שלך"
                     Description="כשצוות יגיש בקשה, היא תופיע כאן." />
    }
    else
    {
        <div class="rqw-split">

            <!-- ══ QUEUE — right column ══════════════════════════════════ -->
            <aside class="rqw-sidebar">

                @* The reference's own two controls, moved off the title row and
                   onto the queue they filter. The tab counts came off with
                   them: the KPI row above now states each number once. *@
                <div class="rqw-filters">

                    <MFilterTabs Tabs="@FilterTabs"
                                 ActiveKey="@ActiveTabKey"
                                 OnSelect="SelectLane"
                                 AriaLabel="סינון בקשות לפי מצב" />

                    @*  The shared type dropdown — same markup, same classes
                        and the same open / pick / close shape the lecturer
                        queue uses. Only the option list is this page's, and it
                        is read off the mentor's own scoped rows.  *@
                    <div class="rqw-type-wrap" @onkeydown="OnTypeKeyDown">
                        <button type="button"
                                class="@TypeButtonClass"
                                aria-haspopup="listbox"
                                aria-expanded="@(_typeOpen ? "true" : "false")"
                                aria-label="סינון לפי סוג בקשה"
                                @onclick="ToggleTypeMenu"
                                @onclick:stopPropagation="true">
                            <span class="rqw-type-label-text">סוג בקשה</span>
                            <span class="rqw-type-val-text">@TypeButtonValue</span>
                            <span class="rqw-type-caret @(_typeOpen ? "rqw-type-caret-open" : "")"
                                  aria-hidden="true">
                                <svg width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
                                     stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"
                                     stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                                    <path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/>
                                </svg>
                            </span>
                        </button>

                        @if (_typeOpen)
                        {
                            <div class="rqw-type-backdrop" @onclick="CloseTypeMenu"></div>

                            <div class="rqw-type-panel" role="listbox" aria-label="סוג בקשה">
                                <button type="button"
                                        class="@TypeOptionClass(null)"
                                        role="option"
                                        aria-selected="@(_typeFilter is null ? "true" : "false")"
                                        @onclick="@(() => PickType(null))">
                                    <span class="rqw-type-opt-label">הכל</span>
                                    @if (_typeFilter is null)
                                    {
                                        <svg class="rqw-type-check" width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
                                             stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6"
                                             stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                                            <path d="m5 12.5 4.5 4.5L19 7"/>
                                        </svg>
                                    }
                                </button>

                                @foreach (var t in AvailableTypes)
                                {
                                    var type = t;
                                    <button type="button"
                                            class="@TypeOptionClass(type)"
                                            role="option"
                                            aria-selected="@(_typeFilter == type ? "true" : "false")"
                                            @onclick="@(() => PickType(type))">
                                        <span class="rqw-type-opt-label">@TypeLabel(type)</span>
                                        @if (_typeFilter == type)
                                        {
                                            <svg class="rqw-type-check" width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
                                                 stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6"
                                                 stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                                                <path d="m5 12.5 4.5 4.5L19 7"/>
                                            </svg>
                                        }
                                    </button>
                                }
                            </div>
                        }
                    </div>

                </div>

                <div class="rqw-list">
                  <div class="rqw-list-inner" role="listbox" aria-label="רשימת בקשות">
                    @{
                        var visibleItems = VisibleItems;
                    }
                    @if (visibleItems.Count == 0)
                    {
                        <p class="rqw-list-empty">אין בקשות תואמות לסינון הנוכחי</p>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        @foreach (var r in visibleItems)
                        {
                            var req = r;
                            var isSelected = _expandedId == req.Id;
                            <button type="button"
                                    class="rqw-row @(isSelected ? "rqw-row-selected" : "")"
                                    role="option"
                                    aria-selected="@isSelected"
                                    aria-label="@($"פתיחת הבקשה {req.Title}")"
                                    @onclick="@(() => SelectRequest(req.Id))">

                                @*  ── HEAD LINE — the shared row anatomy ──
                                    The title flexes and ellipses in place, the
                                    request type is pinned to the far LEFT.
                                    Byte for byte the lecturer queue's head, and
                                    the student's: a request row is one object
                                    across the product.

                                    THE LEADING DOT IS GONE. It carried four
                                    tones — rose / violet for "waiting on you"
                                    at and under the attention threshold, blue
                                    for in flight elsewhere, teal / grey for
                                    resolved / closed — and every one of those
                                    is the BUCKET, which is now the pill the
                                    mentor selected to get this list. A colour
                                    per row restating the tab above it is not a
                                    signal; inside "להמלצתך" it was the same
                                    violet on every row, and inside
                                    "ממתין לאחרים" the same blue.

                                    The one thing the dot said that the tab does
                                    not — that a request has waited past the
                                    attention threshold — is not lost: it is on
                                    the opened record's meta line, in the shared
                                    attention model's own words (recWait), where
                                    it is read once about the request the mentor
                                    actually opened.  *@
                                <div class="rqw-row-head">
                                    <span class="rqw-row-title">@req.Title</span>
                                    <span class="rqw-row-type">@TypeLabel(req.RequestType)</span>
                                </div>

                                @*  ── META — WHOSE request this is, and nothing
                                    else. The lecturer queue's line, with the
                                    project kept beside the team because a
                                    mentor's queue spans several of them.

                                    THE SUBMITTER'S NAME IS GONE. A mentor reads
                                    this queue by TEAM: the recommendation is
                                    about a team's extension, the note goes to
                                    the team, and the same team files several
                                    requests through whichever member is at a
                                    keyboard. Naming the member made two rows
                                    about one team look like two unrelated
                                    matters. It is still on the record — the
                                    head's own meta line leads with it — where
                                    it is detail rather than identity.

                                    NO STATE PHRASE AND NO DATE. The row used to
                                    carry "בבדיקת מרצה · עודכן אחרון · 22.08",
                                    the second half of which is the noisiest
                                    thing that can sit under a title: a date
                                    nobody acts on, differing per row, competing
                                    with the identity beside it. The state half
                                    is the selected tab's job now — see
                                    LaneLabel — and the date is on the record.  *@
                                <div class="rqw-row-meta">
                                    <span class="rqw-row-sub">@RowIdentity(req)</span>
                                </div>

                            </button>
                        }
                    }
                  </div>@* rqw-list-inner *@
                </div>@* rqw-list *@

            </aside>

            <!-- ══ WORKSPACE — left column ═══════════════════════════════ -->
            <main class="rqw-main">

                @if (_expandedId is null)
                {
                    <div class="rqw-empty">
                        <div class="rqw-empty-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                            <svg width="40" height="40" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
                                 stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3"
                                 stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                                <path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/>
                                <polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/>
                                <line x1="16" y1="13" x2="8" y2="13"/>
                                <line x1="16" y1="17" x2="8" y2="17"/>
                                <polyline points="10 9 9 9 8 9"/>
                            </svg>
                        </div>
                        <p class="rqw-empty-title">בחרו בקשה כדי לצפות בפרטים</p>
                        <p class="rqw-empty-sub">פרטי הבקשה יוצגו כאן לאחר הבחירה</p>
                    </div>
                }
                else
                {
                    var selectedRow = _all.FirstOrDefault(x => x.Id == _expandedId);

                    @if (selectedRow is null)
                    {
                        <div class="rqw-empty">
                            <p class="rqw-empty-title">הבקשה לא נמצאה</p>
                        </div>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        @*  ── THE RECORD ─────────────────────────────────
                            THE HEAD BAND IS THE PAGE'S, THE BODY IS THE
                            COMPONENT'S. MentorRequestDetail draws its own
                            compact identity block (`mrd-id`: badges stacked
                            above the title) because the modal on המשימות שלי
                            has nothing but the word "בקשה" above it. On a split
                            workspace that stack is the one thing that made this
                            record read as a different object from the student's
                            and the lecturer's, which put the identity at the
                            reading end and the badges in the opposite corner.

                            So the page passes ShowHeader="false" and draws the
                            shared `.rqw-ws-head` itself. The modal keeps its own
                            header untouched — this changes nothing for the two
                            project workspaces or המשימות שלי, and it needed no
                            change inside the component beyond a parameter it
                            already had.

                            EVERYTHING THE MENTOR CAN DO IS STILL THE
                            COMPONENT'S. It draws the recommendation form and
                            nothing else, which is what keeps the lecturer's
                            אישור / דחייה / החזרה off this page without a second
                            permission check here.  *@
                        var recBucket = MentorRequestBuckets.Of(selectedRow.Status);
                        var recWait   = AttentionFor(selectedRow)?.WaitingLabel;

                        <div class="rqw-card" id="request-@selectedRow.Id">

                            <div class="rqw-ws-head">
                                <div class="rqw-ws-ident">
                                    <h2 class="rqw-ws-title">@selectedRow.Title</h2>
                                    <p class="rqw-ws-submeta">
                                        <span class="rqw-meta-strong">@selectedRow.CreatedByName</span>
                                        @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(selectedRow.TeamName))
                                        {
                                            <span class="rqw-meta-sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
                                            <span>@selectedRow.TeamName</span>
                                        }
                                        @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(selectedRow.ProjectTitle))
                                        {
                                            <span class="rqw-meta-sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
                                            <span>@selectedRow.ProjectTitle</span>
                                        }
                                        <span class="rqw-meta-sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
                                        <span>נפתחה @selectedRow.CreatedAt.IsraelFormat("dd.MM.yyyy")</span>
                                        @if (recWait is { Length: > 0 })
                                        {
                                            @*  How long it has waited QUALIFIES the
                                                status badge opposite; it is not a
                                                fact of its own rank, so it rides the
                                                meta line rather than becoming a
                                                third badge competing with it. The
                                                phrase is the shared attention
                                                model's, passed in, never computed
                                                here.  *@
                                            <span class="rqw-meta-sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
                                            <span class="rqw-meta-strong">@recWait</span>
                                        }
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                                <div class="rqw-ws-badges">
                                    <span class="rqw-type-pill">@TypeLabel(selectedRow.RequestType)</span>
                                    <span class="rqw-ws-state rqw-ws-state-@StateTone(recBucket)">
                                        @MentorRequestBuckets.RowLabel(recBucket)
                                    </span>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <div class="rqw-ws-body mrq-ws-body">
                                <MentorRequestDetail RequestId="@selectedRow.Id"
                                                     Layout="MentorRequestDetail.DetailLayout.Record"
                                                     ShowHeader="false"
                                                     WaitingLabel="@recWait"
                                                     OnChanged="OnRequestChangedAsync" />
                            </div>

                        </div>
                    }
                }

            </main>

        </div>@* rqw-split *@
    }

</div>@* rqw-page *@

@code {
    /// <summary>Deep link a request notification arrives on — it expands that
    /// row and reveals whichever section holds it.</summary>
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "requestId")]
    public int? DeepLinkRequestId { get; set; }

    private List<ProjectRequestRowDto> _all = new();

    /// <summary>Waiting ages for the requests that are actually on this mentor.
    /// One extra GET, and the reason this page cannot word or escalate a request
    /// differently from the rest of the mentor experience.</summary>
    private MentorAttentionDto _attention = new();

    /// <summary>Admin-managed request-type names, by code. Empty until loaded
    /// and empty if the call fails — TypeLabel falls back to the Shared
    /// constant either way, so the tag is never blank.</summary>
    private Dictionary<string, string> _typeNames = new();
    private bool _loading = true;
    private bool _loadError;

    /// <summary>
    /// The selected lane. NON-NULLABLE, and that is the fix for "which
    /// workflow state am I looking at?".
    ///
    /// <para>It used to be a nullable with null as the opening value, meaning
    /// the queue loaded showing "everything except טופלו" with NO pill lit —
    /// a state the filter bar had no way to name, on a list whose rows had
    /// just stopped naming it either. The lecturer queue has never had that
    /// state: its own <c>_activeTab</c> opens on "decision" and is always one
    /// of the three. This is the same rule, and it opens on the same lane —
    /// the one the mentor actually owns.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>Nothing about the lanes, the counts or the ordering changed; the
    /// list simply opens filtered instead of opening unfiltered.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private MentorLane _laneFilter = MentorLane.AwaitingMentor;
    private string?              _typeFilter;
    private int?                 _expandedId;
    private bool                 _typeOpen;

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        await LoadAsync();
        ApplyDeepLink();
    }

    private void ApplyDeepLink()
    {
        if (DeepLinkRequestId is not int id) return;

        var row = _all.FirstOrDefault(r => r.Id == id);
        if (row is null) return;

        _expandedId = id;

        // The queue shows exactly ONE lane now, so a deep link has to bring its
        // own or it selects a row the list is not drawing. It already did this
        // for טופלו, which the old unfiltered opening state hid; every lane
        // needs it once the opening state is a lane of its own.
        _laneFilter = LaneOf(row.Status);
    }

    private async Task LoadAsync()
    {
        _loading = true;
        _loadError = false;

        var rowsTask      = RequestsService.GetAllAsync();
        var attentionTask = Attention.GetAsync();
        var typesTask     = RequestTypesService.GetActiveAsync();
        await Task.WhenAll(rowsTask, attentionTask, typesTask);

        var rows = await rowsTask;
        if (rows is null) { _loadError = true; _loading = false; return; }

        _attention = await attentionTask;

        // The admin-managed display names, exactly as the lecturer queue loads
        // them. GET /api/request-types/active is open to any authenticated user
        // — it is the same call the student's NewRequestModal picker makes — so
        // this adds a read the mentor already had, and no write, no state and
        // no permission.
        var types = await typesTask;
        _typeNames = types is null
            ? new()
            : types.Where(t => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(t.Code))
                   .GroupBy(t => t.Code)
                   .ToDictionary(g => g.Key, g => g.First().Name);

        // Newest activity first, the ordering the legacy inbox used.
        _all = rows.OrderByDescending(r => r.UpdatedAt).ToList();
        _loading = false;
    }

    /// <summary>A recommendation was accepted, so the request has changed
    /// bucket — reload rather than patching one row's status by hand.</summary>
    private async Task OnRequestChangedAsync()
    {
        _expandedId = null;
        await LoadAsync();
    }

    /// <summary>Clicking a row selects it; clicking the selected row clears the
    /// workspace back to its empty state. MentorRequestDetail loads the record
    /// and clears the unread marker itself, so there is nothing to fetch
    /// here.</summary>
    private void SelectRequest(int id) => _expandedId = _expandedId == id ? null : id;

    // ── Filters ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>Changing a filter drops the selection — never auto-selects the
    /// first row. An unparseable key falls back to the opening lane rather than
    /// to "no lane", so the bar can never end up with every pill dark again.
    /// (MFilterTabs only ever emits one of its own keys; this is the guard, not
    /// a path anything takes.)</summary>
    private void SelectLane(string key)
    {
        _laneFilter = Enum.TryParse<MentorLane>(key, out var l) ? l : MentorLane.AwaitingMentor;
        _expandedId = null;
    }

    private void ToggleTypeMenu() => _typeOpen = !_typeOpen;

    private void CloseTypeMenu() => _typeOpen = false;

    private void OnTypeKeyDown(KeyboardEventArgs e)
    {
        if (e.Key == "Escape") _typeOpen = false;
    }

    private void PickType(string? type)
    {
        _typeFilter = type;
        _typeOpen   = false;
        _expandedId = null;
    }

    /// <summary>Always one of the three, so exactly one pill is lit at all
    /// times — the same contract the lecturer queue's ActiveKey has.</summary>
    private string ActiveTabKey => _laneFilter.ToString();

    /// <summary>
    /// להמלצתך · ממתין לאחרים · טופלו — the three lanes, worded from the
    /// mentor's side (see LaneLabel).
    ///
    /// <para>AwaitingMentor and InFlight carry live counts that respect the
    /// current type filter, matching the student and lecturer queues. טופלו
    /// carries none, also matching them: a count of everything ever finished is
    /// not a workload.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<MFilterTabs.Tab> FilterTabs => new[]
    {
        new MFilterTabs.Tab(MentorLane.AwaitingMentor.ToString(), LaneLabel(MentorLane.AwaitingMentor), AwaitingMentorCount),
        new MFilterTabs.Tab(MentorLane.InFlight.ToString(),       LaneLabel(MentorLane.InFlight),       InFlightCount),
        new MFilterTabs.Tab(MentorLane.Closed.ToString(),         LaneLabel(MentorLane.Closed)),
    };

    private int AwaitingMentorCount => Narrowed.Count(r => LaneOf(r.Status) == MentorLane.AwaitingMentor);
    private int InFlightCount       => Narrowed.Count(r => LaneOf(r.Status) == MentorLane.InFlight);

    // ── The lane: the page's ONE fold of MentorRequestBuckets ───────────
    //
    // A mentor has four buckets but only three things they can do about a
    // request: act on it, wait for someone else, or file it. WithLecturer and
    // AwaitingTeam differ in WHO is holding it, not in what the mentor does —
    // both are "בטיפול" — and giving each its own primary tab made a five-pill
    // track that wrapped to two rows in a 340px queue (measured: 335px of pills
    // in 303px of track). So the primary filter is the lane, and the bucket
    // survives as metadata on the row that needs it.
    //
    // THIS IS A FOLD, NOT A SECOND STATUS MAPPING. LaneOf calls
    // MentorRequestBuckets.Of and groups its result; nothing here reads a raw
    // status. Because the KPI chips, the filter tabs and the list all go
    // through this one method, a chip cannot disagree with the tab that
    // selects it or with the rows it shows.

    private enum MentorLane { AwaitingMentor, InFlight, Closed }

    private static MentorLane LaneOf(string status) => MentorRequestBuckets.Of(status) switch
    {
        MentorRequestBucket.AwaitingMentor => MentorLane.AwaitingMentor,
        MentorRequestBucket.Closed         => MentorLane.Closed,
        // WithLecturer + AwaitingTeam — in flight with someone who is not you.
        _                                  => MentorLane.InFlight,
    };

    /// <summary>
    /// What the mentor is being asked for, per lane. Each label answers one
    /// question — "what is expected from me now?" — because with the state
    /// phrase off the rows, the pill is the only thing left that explains why
    /// these requests are in front of the reader.
    ///
    /// <para><b>"בטיפול" became "ממתין לאחרים", and the mapping is what earns
    /// the rename.</b> The old word was ambiguous in the worst direction: it
    /// reads as "someone is working on it" and, on the mentor's own queue,
    /// most naturally as "being handled BY YOU" — which is the one thing it
    /// never meant. LaneOf folds MentorRequestBuckets.WithLecturer and
    /// AwaitingTeam into it, i.e. every status except PendingMentorRecommendation
    /// (its own lane) and Resolved / Closed (the last one). The mentor holds
    /// none of them: the server gives a mentor exactly one decision endpoint,
    /// <c>POST /api/project-requests/{id}/mentor-recommendation</c>, which is
    /// Mentor-only AND gated on PendingMentorRecommendation, so every request
    /// in this lane is literally waiting on the academic side or on the team.
    /// "ממתין לאחרים" is a restatement of that, not a new claim.</para>
    ///
    /// <para><b>"להמלצתך" is kept over the more generic "דורש ממך פעולה".</b>
    /// The lane is one status wide and the action it wants has a name — a
    /// recommendation — so the specific word answers the question better than
    /// the general one, and it is the word the endpoint, the status label
    /// ("ממתינה להמלצת מנחה") and the lecturer's own "בטיפול מנחה" tab already
    /// use for the same moment.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>Which of the two OTHERS is holding a request — the lecturer or
    /// the team — is no longer on the row; MentorRequestBuckets.RowLabel still
    /// says it exactly, on the opened record's status badge. That is the one
    /// thing this lane's fold costs, and the record is where it is read.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>No bucket, no count, no query and no status moved. This is the
    /// word on the pill.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private static string LaneLabel(MentorLane l) => l switch
    {
        MentorLane.AwaitingMentor => "להמלצתך",
        MentorLane.InFlight       => "הועבר לטיפול",
        _                         => "טופלו",
    };

    /// <summary>The control shows a muted "סוג בקשה" caption beside the current
    /// VALUE, so it still says what it filters once a type is picked — and "הכל"
    /// is a real value rather than a blank.</summary>
    private string TypeButtonValue =>
        _typeFilter is null ? "הכל" : TypeLabel(_typeFilter);

    private string TypeButtonClass =>
        _typeFilter is null ? "rqw-type-btn" : "rqw-type-btn rqw-type-btn-active";

    private string TypeOptionClass(string? type) =>
        _typeFilter == type ? "rqw-type-opt rqw-type-opt-on" : "rqw-type-opt";

    /// <summary>
    /// Only the types that actually occur in this mentor's requests — a menu
    /// entry for a type no team ever files is a dead control.
    ///
    /// <para>Read off the DATA and then ordered by the canonical list, not
    /// filtered by it: rows exist whose RequestType is not in
    /// <c>RequestTypes.All</c> (ScopeChange, SpecialResource, Consultation all
    /// appear in the QA seed). Filtering by the constant list dropped those
    /// three out of the control entirely, so there was no way to select them.
    /// RequestTypes.Label already falls back to the raw string.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private List<string> AvailableTypes =>
        _all.Select(r => r.RequestType)
            .Where(t => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(t))
            .Distinct()
            .OrderBy(t =>
            {
                var i = RequestTypes.All.ToList().IndexOf(t);
                return i < 0 ? int.MaxValue : i;
            })
            .ThenBy(t => t, StringComparer.Ordinal)
            .ToList();

    // ── Derived ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>The SECONDARY filter. VisibleItems applies the lane on top of
    /// this, so a type always narrows *within* whichever lane is showing rather
    /// than replacing it — the two controls are independent.</summary>
    private IEnumerable<ProjectRequestRowDto> Narrowed =>
        _all.Where(r => _typeFilter is null || r.RequestType == _typeFilter);

    /// <summary>
    /// The queue, flat: exactly the selected lane, narrowed by the type filter.
    ///
    /// <para>Ordered by bucket first, because MentorRequestBuckets.Ordered is
    /// descending urgency for a mentor — so the requests the mentor actually
    /// owns (מחכות לתגובתך) sit at the top of the list and the ones merely in
    /// flight elsewhere sit below. Newest activity breaks ties within a bucket,
    /// which is the ordering _all already arrives in.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private List<ProjectRequestRowDto> VisibleItems =>
        Narrowed
            .Where(r => LaneOf(r.Status) == _laneFilter)
            .OrderBy(r => BucketRank(MentorRequestBuckets.Of(r.Status)))
            .ThenByDescending(r => r.UpdatedAt)
            .ToList();

    /// <summary>Position in MentorRequestBuckets.Ordered — descending urgency
    /// for a mentor. A lookup rather than a second switch, so the sort follows
    /// the shared order automatically if a bucket is ever added or reordered.
    /// (IReadOnlyList has no IndexOf.)</summary>
    private static int BucketRank(MentorRequestBucket b)
    {
        for (var i = 0; i < MentorRequestBuckets.Ordered.Count; i++)
            if (MentorRequestBuckets.Ordered[i] == b) return i;
        return int.MaxValue;
    }

    // ── Presentation ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// The row's whole identity: "צוות · פרויקט".
    ///
    /// <para>The lecturer queue's TeamIdentity with the project kept beside the
    /// team rather than used only as its fallback, and that difference is the
    /// audience's, not a design divergence: a lecturer reads one cohort, where
    /// the team name identifies a row on its own, while a mentor's queue spans
    /// several projects at once and "צוות 3" in two of them is two different
    /// teams. Both roles draw it as one muted line under the title, in the same
    /// class, so the rows stay the same object.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>CreatedByName was the first item here and is deliberately gone —
    /// see the row's own note. Nothing is computed: both values arrive on the
    /// row DTO the queue already loaded.</para>
    /// </summary>
    /// <summary>
    /// The request type's display name — the lecturer queue's TypeLabel,
    /// verbatim.
    ///
    /// <para>This page printed <c>RequestTypes.Label</c> directly, which is the
    /// Shared constant list. Request types are ADMIN-MANAGED, so a type created
    /// in /management/request-types has no constant and that call returns its
    /// raw code: the same request showed a real Hebrew name on the lecturer's
    /// queue and something like "ExtensionB" on the mentor's. Two words for one
    /// tag on two screens of one feature.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>Presentation only. The dictionary decides how a code is SPELLED;
    /// it never decides which requests exist, which bucket they fall in, or
    /// what may be done to them.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private string TypeLabel(string code) =>
        _typeNames.TryGetValue(code, out var name) && !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(name)
            ? name
            : RequestTypes.Label(code);

    private static string RowIdentity(ProjectRequestRowDto r)
    {
        var parts = new[] { r.TeamName, r.ProjectTitle }
            .Where(v => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(v));

        var line = string.Join(" · ", parts);
        return line.Length > 0 ? line : "—";
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// The record header's status badge, in the shared workspace's colour roles
    /// (`rqw-ws-state-*`). A FOLD OF THE BUCKET, not a second status mapping —
    /// the same four buckets the dot, the lanes and the row label already read.
    ///
    /// <para>AwaitingTeam resolves to <c>brand</c>, never <c>attention</c>: a
    /// request sitting on NeedsInfo is waiting for the STUDENT, and rose on a
    /// mentor's screen would say the mentor owes it a move. That is the shared
    /// ownership rule wearing a colour.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private static string StateTone(MentorRequestBucket b) => b switch
    {
        MentorRequestBucket.AwaitingMentor => "attention",
        MentorRequestBucket.Closed         => "done",
        _                                  => "brand",
    };

    /// <summary>The attention item for a request, or null when it is not waiting
    /// on this mentor. Null is the normal case — most rows on this page are with
    /// the lecturer, with the team, or closed.</summary>
    private MentorAttentionItemDto? AttentionFor(ProjectRequestRowDto r) =>
        _attention.Items.FirstOrDefault(
            i => i.Kind == MentorAttentionKind.Request && i.EntityId == r.Id);
}
